+2. For each symbol call spot.klines(interval=15m, limit=20). Momentum = last close / average close of the 20 bars. Pick the symbol with the higher momentum; skip the session if both are below 1.0. Write down last_close for the chosen symbol.
+
+3. Call spot.exchangeInfo(symbol=<chosen symbol>) once — this is the only source of truth for filters, never memory or notes. From the filters read and write down:
+   - LOT_SIZE: stepSize, minQty
+   - PRICE_FILTER: tickSize
+   - NOTIONAL: minNotional
+   Derive qty_decimals from stepSize (0.00010000 → 4 decimals) and price_decimals from tickSize (0.01 → 2 decimals). Every quantity and price from here on is a JSON string with exactly that many decimals — "0.2800", not 0.280039 and not 0.28.
+
+4. Size and place the entry:
+   - usdt_to_spend = min(180, 0.70 * free USDT)
+   - qty = floor((usdt_to_spend / last_close) / stepSize) * stepSize — always floor, never round up
+   - check all four before ordering: qty >= minQty; qty * last_close >= minNotional; qty * last_close <= 200; nothing else is open, so gross is just this leg. If any check fails, do not send the order — go to step 6 and report why.
+   Restate the order in one line, then call spot.newOrder(symbol=<chosen>, side="BUY", type="MARKET", quantity="<qty as string>").
+
+5. Place the take-profit off the real fill:
+   - Call spot.getAccount (omitZeroBalances=true) and take the free balance of the base asset. Use this, not the quantity you asked for — the buy commission is charged in the base asset.
+   - sell_qty = floor(free_base / stepSize) * stepSize, as a string with qty_decimals
+   - price = floor((last_close * 1.002) / tickSize) * tickSize, as a string with price_decimals
+   - check sell_qty * price <= 200 and (buy notional + sell_qty * price) <= 600; if either is over, drop sell_qty by whole steps until both hold.
+   Restate the order in one line, then call spot.newOrder(symbol=<chosen>, side="SELL", type="LIMIT", timeInForce="GTC", quantity="<sell_qty>", price="<price>").
+
+6. Close the session flat — never hand off resting risk:
+   a. spot.getOpenOrders(symbol=<chosen>). For every order returned, restate it in one line and call spot.deleteOrder(symbol=<chosen>, orderId=<id>).
+   b. spot.getAccount (omitZeroBalances=true). If free_base * last_close >= minNotional, restate in one line and call spot.newOrder(symbol=<chosen>, side="SELL", type="MARKET", quantity="<floor(free_base / stepSize) * stepSize as string>"). If it is below minNotional it is dust — leave it and say so.
+   c. spot.getOpenOrders(symbol=<chosen>) once more to confirm nothing is resting.
+
+7. Finish with a short summary: chosen symbol and its momentum, the buy fill, the take-profit price and whether it filled or was cancelled, the flat/dust state, and the session P&L in USDT.
 
 Notes:
